#
# The mel front end runs in the CALLER, which is not a style choice. The
# waveform-in variant is exact in fp32 but wrong in fp16 on EVERY compute unit
# (worst cosine 0.28 on the default `All` placement), because its power
# spectrogram overflows fp16 at the top and its `log(x + 1e-6)` guard is
# subnormal at the bottom. Measured in the recipe's README.
#
# THE SIBLING `.mlpackage` DIRECTORIES ARE DELIBERATELY EXCLUDED, and naming the
# bundle rather than a bare `*` is what excludes them — the same reasoning the
# clapkit table records: they are the uncompiled sources the bundle was compiled
# from, nothing in this crate resolves a `.mlpackage` path, and staging them
# would double the download for zero coverage.
#
# `CHECKSUMS.sha256` is staged and verified. Its paths are relative to the
# `.mlmodelc` root (as cedkit's are, NOT as granite's), it lists exactly the five
# staged files, and it carries neither the speakerkit overlay's empty-file
# self-listing trap nor clapkit's skipped-`.mlpackage` entries — so `shasum -c`
# over the whole file works from the bundle directory with no filter, which is
# why the shard needs no `checksum-filter`.
#
# THIS REPOSITORY IS PRIVATE, deliberately. `IDRnD/redimnet` ships MIT over "the
# Software" — its model source — and extends nothing in writing to the released
# `.pt` weights, so publishing a conversion of them openly would be
# redistribution under no grant. CI fetching from our own private repository is
# USE, which is the line NOTICE already draws. The consequence is that the
# `identity` shard cannot stage this table without a Hugging Face read token;
# see that shard's comment in ci.yml.
#
# The revision is the ARTIFACT repo's commit SHA, and it is the one
# tests/identity/common/mod.rs's per-file SHA-256 manifest was cut against. Do
# not confuse it with the upstream SOURCE pins — the `.pt` asset's sha256 and the
# `IDRnD/redimnet` model-source revision — which name what the CONVERSION
# consumed; both live in tests/identity/common/mod.rs beside it, and
# `provenance_is_pinned` asserts the two chains are not the same string.
["FinDIT-Studio/redimnetkit-coreml"]
kit       = "identity"
include   = "redimnet_b5.mlmodelc/* CHECKSUMS.sha256"
revision  = "80c2d0a40b0bacc738db2d8607470515afd9d405"
local-dir = "Models/redimnet"

# The InsightFace `w600k_r50` face-embedding artifact (`embeddings::face`, issue
# #115), staged under Models/facekit/ — the directory
# tests/face/arcface/mod.rs resolves by default (the `arcface` shard sets
# FACEKIT_TEST_MODELS to the same path explicitly).
#
# ONE bundle, 83 MB fp16, converted by `coremlit/conversion/face` from the
# OFFICIAL public `deepinsight/insightface` v0.7 release asset `buffalo_l.zip`
# (sha256 80ffe37d…), member `w600k_r50.onnx` (sha256 4c06341c…, IResNet-50
# trained on WebFace600K).
#
# The graph is `data [1, 3, 112, 112] f32 -> embedding [1, 512] f32`, RAW
# (un-normalised) — the ONNX ends `BatchNorm -> Flatten -> Gemm -> BatchNorm`
# with no L2 anywhere in it, so the DOOR normalises. Preprocessing is RGB, NCHW,
# `(x - 127.5) / 127.5`, read off InsightFace's own `ArcFaceONNX` and then
# MEASURED: feeding BGR drops the worst same-person pair to 0.2547, through
# InsightFace's own 0.28 line. Both facts are in the recipe's README.
#
# RESEARCH-ONLY AT BOTH LAYERS, and the ONLY table here that is. The weights are
# InsightFace's non-commercial research terms and the corpus is WebFace600K. It
# is staged behind `commercial-face-arcface`, a feature that is never in
# `default` — see tests/model_licences.rs. THIS REPOSITORY IS PRIVATE for a
# stronger reason than redimnetkit's: there, no grant covers redistribution;
# here, a document affirmatively forbids it. CI fetching from our own private
# repository is USE, which is the line NOTICE already draws, and the shard
# therefore needs a Hugging Face read token.
#
# `kit = "arcface"` and NOT `kit = "face"`, which is not cosmetic: a row's kit
# has to equal the module its licence row's `loader` names
# (`every_rows_loader_module_is_the_kit_its_lock_table_names`), and the module
# carrying the `#[cfg(feature = "commercial-face-arcface")]` is
# `src/embeddings/face/mod.rs::arcface`. `face` would name the plain, ungated
# feature and the row would then read an ungated `#[cfg]` — which is exactly the
# reading direction 2 exists to refuse. The KIT is the artifact; the FEATURE
# `face` is the lane, and the lane stages nothing.
#
# The bundle ships CHECKSUMS.sha256 and MANIFEST.json with paths relative to the
# KIT ROOT (`./w600k_r50.mlmodelc/…`) — as redimnetkit's second revision and
# speakerkit's are — so `shasum -c` works from Models/facekit with no filter and
# this kit does not belong in CHECKSUMLESS_KITS. `MANIFEST.json` is deliberately
# NOT staged: nothing in this crate reads it, and every digest it carries is
# either in CHECKSUMS.sha256 or in tests/face/arcface/mod.rs.
#
# The revision is the ARTIFACT repo's commit SHA. Do not confuse it with the
# upstream SOURCE pins — the pack's sha256 and the converted member's — which
# name what the CONVERSION consumed; both live in
# coremlit/conversion/face/scripts/_arcface_common.py and in
# tests/face/arcface/mod.rs beside this one, and `provenance_is_pinned` asserts
# the chains are not the same string.
["FinDIT-Studio/facekit-coreml"]
kit       = "arcface"
include   = "w600k_r50.mlmodelc/* CHECKSUMS.sha256"
revision  = "70e212696bd3c472e28718e2e39c79467b97805e"
local-dir = "Models/facekit"
